Для доступа к S3 через IAM policy мы выдаём минимальные права на bucket и prefix. Пример:
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:PutObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::ml-artifacts-bucket/models/*"
    }
  ]
}
```

Сделали service discovery через Consul: сервисы регистрируются в локальном agent, проверки здоровья HTTP `/health` каждые 10s. `consul-template` генерирует конфиг прокси из каталога Consul.

Пример шаблона:
```hcl
{{ range services }}
upstream {{ .Name }} {
  {{ range service .Name }}server {{ .Address }}:{{ .Port }} max_fails=3 fail_timeout=5s;{{ end }}
}
{{ end }}
```

BIND9 (current) named.conf:
```
options {
  recursion no;
  allow-recursion { none; };
};
```
Authoritative-only; no recursive resolution on this server.

BIND9 (old) named.conf:
```
options {
  recursion yes;
  allow-recursion { 10.0.0.0/8; 192.168.0.0/16; };
};
```
We used it as an internal resolver.

Nomad (current): jobs run with bridge networking to isolate allocations; services expose only declared ports via the Nomad network stanza and we avoid host networking except for low-level agents.
Example snippet:
```
group "api" {
  network {
    mode = "bridge"
    port "http" { to = 8080 }
  }
}
```

Edge firewall policy is implemented with nftables (not iptables). Minimal ruleset (IPv4) we ship:

```nft
flush ruleset

table inet filter {
  chain input {
    type filter hook input priority 0; policy drop;
    ct state established,related accept
    iif "lo" accept
    tcp dport {22,443} accept
    udp dport 53 accept
    ip protocol icmp accept
  }

  chain forward {
    type filter hook forward priority 0; policy drop;
    ct state established,related accept
    # block noisy L2 name discovery between VLANs
    udp dport {5353,5355} drop   # mDNS, LLMNR
    # allow DNS + HTTPS from app VLAN to infra VLAN
    iifname "vlan_app" oifname "vlan_infra" tcp dport 443 accept
    iifname "vlan_app" oifname "vlan_infra" udp dport 53 accept
  }
}
```
This specifically prevents cross-segment mDNS/LLMNR chatter while keeping required DNS/HTTPS paths.
